The raster branch builds SQL by string-concatenating `self.ewkb` into a quoted literal. `self.ewkb` comes from `to_pgraster(obj)`, which hexlifies binary raster data (via `binascii.hexlify(...).upper()` and `pack()`), producing an uppercase hex string. Because the value is hex-encoded, it cannot contain a single quote, so it cannot break out of the `'...'` literal — the dynamic content is effectively constrained to `[0-9A-F]`. This is not a bound parameter, but the encoding makes injection infeasible. The geometry branch uses psycopg2's `Binary` adapter (properly quoted). No attacker-controllable value reaches the SQL text unescaped.

